# Trivy IaC scan suppressions.
# Each entry must carry an expiry date — no silent forever-suppressions.
# Format: AVD-XXX-XXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD reason:<one line>
#
# Example:
# AVD-AWS-0123 exp:2026-12-31 reason:false positive in node-bootstrap vendor_data template

AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-07-07 reason:aws-control-plane/aws-node-pool egress destinations (registry_mirror_url, gitops_*_repo_url) are consumer-supplied and arbitrary, not enumerable at plan time or stable enough to CIDR-scope (CDN-backed hosts). This check only inspects CIDR breadth, not port, so port-scoping cannot clear it. Genuine domain-based egress restriction requires a separate network-layer control (NAT + firewall with FQDN allowlisting) that this module deliberately does not create — this project's modules never create network fabric. Unrestricted egress is also the AWS default security-group behavior.

AVD-AWS-0132 exp:2027-07-29 reason:aws-control-plane/aws-node-pool's ansible_ssm bucket is a transient staging area for the amazon.aws.aws_ssm Ansible connection plugin — public access fully blocked, objects expire after 1 day, force_destroy on. SSE-S3 (AES256) already encrypts it at rest; a customer-managed KMS key would add a new piece of fabric (key + key policy + IAM grants) this project deliberately avoids provisioning for data that never outlives a single apply.
